Project Name: Personal Finance Analyzer

Description:
This project is a Python-based personal finance application designed to
analyze bank-exported XLSX transaction statements and transform raw
transaction data into structured financial summaries, visualizations, and
AI-generated insights.

The application supports selecting, validating, and combining multiple bank
statements. It cleans transaction data, determines the reporting period,
classifies income, expenses, transfers, and zero-amount transactions, assigns
financial categories, calculates overall and monthly summaries, calculates
the savings rate, and identifies known subscription spending.

The application generates a one-page landscape financial report containing a
financial summary table, monthly income and expense charts, transaction-count
charts, an expense-category chart, and structured AI Financial Insights.
Savings Rate is presented as an objective percentage in the Financial Summary
table and explained in the existing AI Financial Summary insight. It is not
used to assign a financial-health status or classification.

The completed financial report can be previewed and saved as a PDF. This
project provides hands-on experience working with real-world financial data
while developing skills in Python programming, file handling, data
validation, Pandas data analysis, NumPy calculations, Matplotlib
visualization, financial-data modeling, OpenAI API integration, exception
handling, and software engineering.

Objectives:

Verify that one or more bank-exported XLSX statements can be selected,
validated, opened, and combined successfully.
Verify that required transaction columns are identified correctly.
Verify that transaction dates are processed and the reporting period is
determined accurately.
Verify that transaction amounts are cleaned and converted into valid
numeric values.
Verify that transactions are classified correctly as income, expenses,
transfers, or zero-amount transactions.
Verify that transactions are assigned to the appropriate financial
categories.
Verify that total income, total expenses, net balance, transaction count,
and savings rate are calculated correctly.
Verify that the savings rate is rounded to two decimal places and displayed
as N/A when total income is zero.
Verify that monthly income, expense, transfer, and transaction summaries
are calculated accurately.
Verify that known subscription payments are identified and summarized
correctly.
Verify that the Financial Summary table contains accurate transaction,
income, expense, net-balance, and savings-rate values.
Verify that monthly income and expense charts, transaction-count charts,
and expense-category charts are generated and styled correctly.
Verify that expense-category values representing less than ten percent are
not labeled inside the pie chart.
Verify that the charts and AI insights fit within the one-page landscape
report without overlapping or cutting off content.
Verify that financial data is prepared and validated correctly before
being provided to the AI model.
Verify that AI-generated financial insights follow the required structure,
explain the savings rate in the Financial Summary insight, and use only the
prepared financial data.
Verify that the AI Financial Insights are arranged correctly across the
report and that subscription information remains fully visible.
Verify that generated financial reports can be saved successfully as PDF
files.
Verify that invalid, missing, nonnumeric, nonfinite, or inconsistent
financial data is handled safely with appropriate exceptions and error
messages.
